:: day_2_2_lumira

Her dorm door opens before I can knock. Ava stands there wrapped in her blanket, hair messy, eyes swollen from crying she probably tried to hide. She steps back wordlessly, letting me in.

The moment the door clicks shut, she folds into me   no hesitation, no soft approach like usual. Just a quiet collapse into my chest.

<<ava "I’m sorry… about last night… about everything…">>

She clings like she’s afraid to let go. I hold her gently, rubbing small circles on her back until her breathing evens out.

<<leo "You don’t need to apologize. Not for anything." >>

She shakes her head against me.

<<ava "I keep ruining things… you shouldn’t have to deal with me being like this…">>

God, it hurts hearing her talk about herself this way.

<<leo "Ava, stop. You’re not ruining anything. I’m here because I want to be." >>

She nods, but it’s the kind of nod people do when they don’t believe the words yet.When we leave for breakfast, she stays glued to my side.  

[[Go to Breakfast|day_2_3_lumira]]

:: day_2_3_lumira

At the café, she does something she’s never done before   she slides into the booth nearly on top of me, thigh pressed tightly against mine, shoulder leaned into my chest.

She acts like she doesn’t notice how close she is. But her eyes keep flickering to my face, reading every tiny reaction. I tear off the top of her muffin like always. She tries to smile, but it looks stretched, worried.

<<ava "Thank you…">>

She lifts her tea with both hands, sipping without letting go of me. Her knee nudges mine. She scoots closer. It’s subtle, but desperate like she thinks closeness will erase everything that hurt her yesterday.

<<leo "You can relax, you know. I’m not upset." >>

She stares at the table, fingers fidgeting with the sleeve of my hoodie.

<<ava "I just… I want today to be better. For you.">>

That hits me wrong   too heavy, too self-punishing.

<<leo "Ava, I don’t need you to fix anything." >>

She swallows hard. I can see tears gathering, the kind she won’t let fall in public.

<<ava "But I want to. I want to try harder.">>

She leans her head against my shoulder   not the shy, gentle kind she usually gives me, but something anxious, searching. She keeps touching me in little ways, brushing her fingers along my arm, straightening my sleeve, resting her hand on my thigh for a second before pulling it back like she’s afraid she crossed a line.

She’s trying too hard. Trying to make up for something I never expected from her in the first place. I want to tell her she doesn’t have to do any of this. But she looks up at me with those soft, guilty eyes and whispers,

<<ava "Please don’t be unhappy with me today…">>

It breaks something in me. I put my arm around her shoulders and pull her closer, kissing the top of her head.

<<leo "Ava, I’m not unhappy with you. I never am." >>

She nods again   but the fear doesn’t quite leave her posture. Breakfast ends with her practically tucked under my arm, clinging like letting go might make the entire day fall apart.

<<link "Go to Classess">><<goto leo_class_lumira>><</link>>



:: day_2_4_lumira

After lunch, Ava walks beside me with that same quiet tension wrapped around her shoulders. She doesn’t speak much   just small nods, tiny glances up at me, her hand brushing mine like she’s debating whether she’s allowed to hold it.

When we reach the campus fork, she stops. Her fingers tug nervously at her ribbon. Her voice trembles before the words even form.

<<ava "Um… could I… come to your dorm? Just us?">>

My chest tightens. Something about her tone isn’t excitement   it’s fear mixed with determination.

<<leo "Yeah, of course. We can just relax ">>

<<ava "No  I… I wanted to… do something. For you.">>

Her eyes dart down. Her cheeks burn and that guilt that hasn’t left her since yesterday rises again like a shadow behind her. I reach for her hand.

<<leo "Ava, you don’t have to ">>

She pulls her fingers away gently, shaking her head.

<<ava "I want to. I want to make you happy." >>

The way she says it isn’t desire. It’s obligation. It hits me wrong, but she’s already stepping closer, already fighting some internal battle I can’t interrupt.

