:: day_2_5_lumira

My dorm is quiet when we enter. She closes the door behind us as if sealing herself into a decision she can’t back out of.

She stands still for a moment, breathing unsteadily. Then she turns to me with a fragile little smile that doesn’t reach her eyes.

<<ava "C-Can you… sit down?">>

I sit on the edge of the bed. She takes a step closer. Then another. Her hands tremble as she reaches the hem of her sweater, gripping it so tightly the fabric strains. I shake my head softly.

<<leo "Ava, you don’t need to do anything you don’t want ">>

She cuts me off in a whisper.

<<ava "I want to try. Please… let me try.">>

She lifts the sweater just a little   not fully, just enough that the loose neckline dips. Enough that a soft curve shows at the edge of her bra. Enough that the slightest movement reveals a shy, trembling peek of her nipple. Her voice cracks.

<<ava "Y-You can… look. If you want to.">>

My heart twists. She’s blushing so hard she can’t meet my eyes. She’s doing this for me not because she’s ready, but because she thinks she has to compensate for yesterday.

She steps between my knees and takes my hand in both of hers. Her palms are freezing.

<<ava "I know you… want more. And I keep messing up. I just… want to make you feel good. Once." >>

Before I can tell her she’s wrong, she kneels. Her fingers fumble with my zipper. She’s shaking so much she misses twice before getting it. I swallow, guilt already coiling in my gut.

<<leo "Ava… we can stop. You don’t have to ">>

<<ava "I-I’m okay. I promise. I want to.">>

Her eyes flick open for half a second, widen, then shut again fast like she wasn’t prepared for what she saw. But her voice is too small to be a promise. She pulls my penis out carefully, eyes squeezing shut as if afraid of looking directly. Her hand wraps around my penis, timid and awkward and terrified.

<<ava "Oh  um… oh." >>

She bites her lip, cheeks burning, fingers frozen around the base like she’s afraid she’s holding it wrong. It is first time Ava seeing me penis. I can see her awkwardly look. She is handling it very unfamiliar way. 

<<ava "I… I didn’t think it would look like this.">>

She retreats her gaze immediately, like she’s embarrassed by her own curiosity.

<<ava "It feels large in my hand. It is bigger than I thought...">>

Her grip shifts awkwardly, unsure where to hold, how tight, how gentle. The first stroke is barely pressure at all. The second is shaky, uneven. She’s breathing fast   not arousal, but panic.

<<ava "It’s… um… warmer">>

Her fingers test the warmth like she’s unsure if she’s allowed to touch at all. She swallows hard. Her voice shakes like she’s reporting data she doesn’t know how to interpret.

<<ava "Am I… doing it right?">>

<<leo "Ava, you don’t need to ">>

<<ava "Please  just… let me.">>

Her hand keeps moving, guided more by obligation than instinct. I want to stop her. I should stop her. But she looks so desperate to prove something to fix something that was never broken that I freeze.

The guilt smothers me even as pleasure coils tightly, too fast, too wrong. Her eyes stay closed the whole time. She never looks at me.

I finish   quickly, helplessly   more from shock than release, feeling sick with how wrong it feels. Ava gasps softly when warmth hits her fingers.  

She pulls her hand back like she’s been burned, staring at her palm in trembling disbelief before wiping it hastily with a tissue from my desk. She won’t meet my eyes.

<<ava "I… I hope that… made you happy." >>

Her smile is paper-thin. Her fingers still shake. She stands abruptly, hugging herself like she’s cold.

<<leo "Ava  wait  we should talk ">>

She shakes her head, already stepping toward the door.

<<ava "I-I need to go. I forgot  I have something to do. I’m sorry  I’m so sorry ">>

Before I can stand up, before I can say anything, she’s already slipping out the door, closing it softly behind her. The room feels too quiet without her and the guilt sits in my chest like a stone.

<<link "Answer Call">><<goto day_2_6_lumira>><</link>>


:: day_2_6_lumira

My phone buzzes just as I’m trying to clear my head. Ava’s name appears on the screen. I hesitate before answering not because I don’t want to talk, but because I’m scared of what she’s feeling right now. Her voice is tiny when I pick up.

<<ava "H-Hi… um… I… I’m sorry.">>

She swallows audibly.

<<ava "I left your room so fast. I didn’t say anything. I didn’t even… look at you. I’m really, really sorry.">>

I close my eyes, guilt pressing down again.

<<leo "Ava, you don’t need to apologize. I just want to make sure you’re okay.">>

There’s a trembling little breath on the other end.

<<ava "I’m… I’m okay. I think. Or I’m trying to be. I didn’t mean to run out like that. I just… felt weird. And embarrassed. And wrong.">>

My chest tightens.

<<leo "You didn’t do anything wrong." >>

But she goes quiet   quiet in that way where she clearly doesn’t believe me. After a moment, she speaks again, softer.

<<ava "Can we… maybe… do something normal today? Like go out? I don’t want things to… stay heavy.">>

I lean back on my bed, heart aching.

<<leo "Yeah. Of course. What do you want to do?">>

Another shaky inhale.

