<<leo "Yeah. You're doing fine." >>

A tiny relieved breath leaves her lips. Then   to my shock   she leans in. Her mouth brushes the tip. Just a small, warm, trembling lick. A sound escapes her   not panic, not disgust, something like *startled confusion.* She tries again.

Her tongue touches the tip for maybe five seconds and then she jerks back suddenly. Like something electric startled her. Her eyes widen. Her breath stutters. Her hands pull into her chest.

<<leo "Ava? What is it?" >>

She shakes her head quickly, almost frantically.

<<ava "I… I’m sorry, I I can’t something felt " >>

She doesn’t finish the sentence. She curls in on herself slightly, arms wrapped tight, shaking. Not crying. Just overwhelmed. Just frightened by her own courage. I zip myself quietly, sit beside her, but she won’t lift her head.

<<leo "It’s okay. You’re okay. We’re done. No pressure." >>

She nods, but her breath is still uneven.

<<ava "You should… go rest. I don’t want to make things weird." >>

I want to argue, to stay, to comfort her more but she’s folded too tightly into herself. She needs space more than reassurance. I stand slowly. She whispers without looking up,

<<ava "Goodnight… Leo." >>

I linger a moment, then finally step out. The door closes softly behind me. I walk toward my dorm with my thoughts buzzing, my heart tight, and that strange phantom dream warmth still humming through my body unwelcome, confusing, too vivid. Tonight is going to be a long night.

<<link "Go to Dorm">><<goto day_3_11_lumira>><</link>>


:: day_3_11_lumira

Back in my dorm, the room feels too quiet. The lights, the familiar smell, the unmade bed   everything feels a little off, a little disoriented.

Maybe because Ava tried again tonight. Maybe because she panicked again. Maybe because I still keep feeling phantom warmth where nothing should be warm at all. I exhale, rub my face, and sit on the edge of my bed. My phone buzzes. Rowan. I answer.

<<leo "Hey. What’s up?" >>

He doesn’t waste time.

<<rowan "Jamie told me everything. About Ava. And the VR thing. Thought you might want help figuring it out." >>

I slump a little in relief.

<<leo "Yeah. Honestly… I could use it." >>

There’s shuffling on his end then Jamie’s voice appears in the background, loud enough to hear but not directly in the call.

<<jamie "Tell him it’s not some weird hookup thing! Tell him it’s legit therapy-level!" >>

Rowan mutters something, amused.

<<rowan "You heard her. It’s legit. And yeah   Jamie and I use it too. Still do." >>

I blink.

<<leo "Still? Even now?" >>

<<rowan "Yeah. Especially since she’s abroad half the year. It keeps us connected. Emotionally. Physically. All of it." >>

Jamie pipes up again, closer this time.

<<jamie "It feels real, Leo! Like real real. Warmth, touch, everything. But without panic. Without pressure." >>

Rowan sighs playfully.

<<rowan "She won’t let me explain anything without jumping in. But… she’s right. The system’s insane. Fully immersive. Your brain buys it completely." >>

My heart beats a little faster. A safe place. A pressure-free place. A place where Ava won’t freeze up.

<<leo "And you think it could help Ava?" >>

Rowan’s tone softens.

<<rowan "Yeah, man. I do. She’s not broken. She’s scared. And VR lets her be close without her body freaking out." >>

Jamie again:

<<jamie "Tell him about the sensitivity adjuster!" >>

<<rowan "Right, right   there’s an intensity slider. You can control how real it feels. You can go slow. Very slow. Ava can decide every setting." >>

That part lands heavily. Ava in full control.

<<leo "That… actually sounds perfect for her." >>

Jamie’s voice grows warm.

<<jamie "Ava’s trying so hard. Don’t let her feel guilty for needing help. Let the VR take the pressure off both of you." >>

I nod to myself. A quiet moment follows. Then Rowan says,

<<rowan "We’ll come with you two tomorrow. Help you pick the room, get everything installed, walk you through setup." >>

<<leo "You sure? It’s a lot of trouble ">>

<<rowan "Leo. We care about Ava. And we care about you. It’s not trouble." >>

Jamie adds,

<<jamie "Tomorrow morning! We’ll meet you at the plaza. Don’t let him oversleep." >>

I smirk.

<<leo "Got it." >>

Rowan chuckles.

<<rowan "Get some rest, man. Tomorrow’s a big step. For both of you." >>

<<leo "Yeah. Thanks… really." >>

The call ends. I lie back on my bed, staring at the ceiling. My body feels strange   not bad, not good, just… not quite mine.

A leftover echo of a dream I shouldn’t remember so vividly. Ava’s voice whispering my name in a way no one ever has. The warmth between my thighs that doesn’t exist. That soft, unreal shift I shake my head, exhale slowly.

Tomorrow is real. Tomorrow is what matters. Not the dream. Not the weird phantom sensations. Tomorrow, Ava and I take a step together.

<<link "Continue to Day 4 – VR Start">><<goto Day4_VRStart>><</link>>
